# Docker build-context exclusions. Honored when `docker build` is invoked
# with the repo root as context (`docker build -f scripts/e2e-linux/Dockerfile.<distro> .`).
#
# Without these, COPY . /repo pulls multi-GB of node_modules + lock files
# carrying corporate-proxy-rewritten tarball URLs (Netskope on the
# maintainer's machine), and `npm install` inside the container fails
# with SELF_SIGNED_CERT_IN_CHAIN against the corporate registry.

# Bulk artifacts — would balloon the build context to multi-GB.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.git
.github
coverage
**/coverage
frontend/.svelte-kit
frontend/build
frontend/test-results
frontend/playwright-report
.planning
docs/superpowers
*.log
.DS_Store

# Host-generated lock files carry corporate-proxy-rewritten tarball URLs
# (e.g. pkgproxy-uat.coinswitch.co) that the Linux containers don't trust.
# Let `npm install` in the container generate a fresh lock against the
# default public registry instead.
package-lock.json
**/package-lock.json
npm-shrinkwrap.json

# Local .npmrc may also pin a corporate registry — exclude defensively
# so containers always use the public registry.
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
